    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0215" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2582</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé Wheeler
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-05T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 1, 11 p.m. The Department yesterday gave to correspondent of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nichi Nichi</hi> a statement denying all charges which
                    you quote from that and other papers. You may call the attention of the Foreign
                    Office to the reported statement of the Chief of the Political Bureau and say
                    that as there is no foundation for such a suspicion <pb facs="0216" n="50"
                        xml:id="pg50"/> the American Government regrets that a responsible Japanese
                    official should attempt to create prejudice against the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
